<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116101" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠκύ-ᾰλος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, perh. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sea-swift,
				speeding o'er the sea,</i> epith. of a ship, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				15.705
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				12.182
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				15.473
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				710
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Mosch.
				2.60
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> later,
			generally, <i>swift, violent,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥιπή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					2.535
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>Parth.</u>
				2.19
			</span></i>. (It is doubtful whether <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-αλος</span> comes from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅλς;</span>
			see opinions of <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
			</span></i> and Hdn.Gr. ap. Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> l.c.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
